{{Quote|It's those womp rats again. Are they trying to chew up all the cables on the planet or what?|Luke Skywalker, after shooting a womp rat|<ref name="LINE">[[Star Wars (LINE Webtoon)|''Star Wars'' LINE Webtoon]]</ref>}}
'''Womp rats''' were creatures native to [[Tatooine]], and were considered pests by local [[moisture farmer]]s who hunted them for sport.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Womp_rat_Alien_Archive.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A womp rat]]
{{Quote|I used to bull's-eye womp rats in my T-16 back home. They're not much bigger than two meters.|Luke Skywalker|<ref name="ANH" />}}
Native to [[Tatooine]], the womp rat evolved to withstand harsh [[desert]] climates. A breed of [[rodent]],<ref name="Alien Archive" /> they were considered [[hair]]y, monstrous pests.<ref name="ANH Illustrated">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref> They had lumpish, [[Color|gray]] skin with tufts of spiky black hair running along their backs. They moved on four legs tipped with three-clawed paws, and had long tails and ears.<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> Typically not much bigger than two [[meter]]s,<ref name="ANH" /> they possessed big, sharp fangs used to seize prey,<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> and had large, yellow eyes.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Behavior==
[[File:WompRatSunning-BoBFCh5.png|thumb|right|300px|A womp rat sunning itself in Beggar's Canyon.]]
Womp rats were not timid creatures,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> hunting in packs and using their fangs to seize prey. When alone, a single womp rat was known to devour the garbage left by moisture farmers.<ref name="Absolutely Everything" /> They lived in the [[Jawa Heights]] region<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> and used [[Beggar's Canyon]] as their den, alongside the more fearsome [[krayt dragon]]s.<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> The smell of [[Death|dead]] womp rats was known to attract krayts. Nesting in the [[desert]], womp rats sometimes gathered in swarms to attack the inhabitants of Tatooine,<ref name="Commander Gameplay">{{YouTube|video=oJkOxsitx5A|text=Star Wars Commander - iOS / Android - HD (Sneak Peek - Empire) Gameplay Trailer|channel=channel/UCfelpouIc8hS7cBXnVKRBpQ|name=TouchGameplay}}</ref> and while these dangerous swarms were feared, inhabitants didn't hesitate to hunt the creatures for sport.<ref name="Geektionary" />

==History==
Womp rats evolved in the harsh desert climate of Tatooine, where they gathered in packs to attack locals. [[Tusken Raider]]s used womp rat tusks to decorate their [[clothing]], and native [[dewback]]s were known to eat the critters.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

During the [[Clone Wars]], when [[Anakin Skywalker]] was having trouble getting information out of [[Doctor|Dr.]] [[Nuvo Vindi]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] told him to have patience, as there was "more than one way to skin a womp rat."<ref name="TCW">{{TCW|Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref>

While living on Tatooine, [[Luke Skywalker]] used his [[T-16 skyhopper]] to hunt womp rats,<ref name="ANH" /> blasting them with the vehicle's pneumatic projectile gun<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref> in the desert world's [[Jawa Heights]] region.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> Luke had the most hits on the monstrous pests of any of his group of friends on a skyhopper run through [[Beggar's Canyon]].<ref name="ANH Illustrated" /> Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], when [[Col Takbright]] protested that the two-[[meter]] target on the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] was impossible to hit even for a [[computer]], Skywalker countered that he used to "bulls-eye" womp rats that were not much bigger than two meters.<ref name="ANH" />

In [[3 ABY]], a [[Pyke]] was attacked by several womp rats while trying to find [[Jawa|Jawas]]. When the thief [[Kay Vess]] found the Pyke, he asked her for [[bacta]] to treat the wound caused by the rat bite, which had become infected. The situation could either help Kay improve her reputation with the [[Pyke Syndicate]], or worsen it, since the Pyke stated he would reveal that she didn't help him if that happened.<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="BOBFDate">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> a womp rat attacked [[BD-72|Peli Motto's BD unit]]. When [[Peli Motto]] attempted to rescue the droid, the womp rat attacked her too. [[Din Djarin]] had arrived and shot the womp rat, [[Death|killing]] it. Later, a womp rat was present in Beggar's Canyon when Djarin tested his modified [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|N-1 starfighter]]. The rat escaped when the [[starfighter]] flew nearby.<ref name="Return of Mandalorian">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>

